From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: give the capture window a click outside when the X focus leaves

Purpose: close an open combo box list when the user clicks elsewhere on
the desktop, also on the application's own taskbar button.
Windows behavior: a click outside the foreground application goes to the
window that has the mouse capture; a combo box's list (the capture
window) closes on a click outside it.
Wine before: under a window manager the click goes to the other X client.
Clicking the desktop or another window changed the foreground and the list
closed, but the application's own taskbar button kept it in the
foreground (Windows 7's taskbar does nothing for a window with a modal
dialog), and the list stayed open. WM_CANCELMODE went to the foreground
window only, which does not have the capture.
Change: with an external shell, when the foreground window loses the X
focus and a window of its thread has the capture (not for moving, sizing
or a menu), that window gets WM_LBUTTONDOWN and WM_LBUTTONUP at the
pointer's position if the pointer is outside it.
Evidence: Wine's Notepad, Open dialog, "files of type" list open: a click
on Notepad's taskbar button in the Windows 7 session left it open, and
closes it after the change; choosing an item with the mouse and the
keyboard still works.
Scope: external shells (WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL).
---
 dlls/winex11.drv/event.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
index 195f2f0..34cb33e 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
@@ -868,6 +868,29 @@ static BOOL X11DRV_FocusIn( HWND hwnd, XEvent *xev )
     return TRUE;
 }
 
+/* win4wine: Windows gives a click outside the foreground application to the
+ * window that has the mouse capture, and a combo box closes its list on it.
+ * Under a window manager the click goes to the other X client (the shell's
+ * taskbar) and the application may keep the foreground, as when its own
+ * taskbar button is clicked: give the capture window a click where the
+ * pointer is when the X focus leaves. */
+static void click_outside_capture(void)
+{
+    GUITHREADINFO info = { .cbSize = sizeof(info) };
+    POINT pt;
+    RECT rect;
+
+    if (!win4wine_external_shell()) return;
+    if (!NtUserGetGUIThreadInfo( GetCurrentThreadId(), &info ) || !info.hwndCapture) return;
+    if (info.flags & (GUI_INMOVESIZE | GUI_INMENUMODE)) return;
+    if (!NtUserGetCursorPos( &pt )) return;
+    NtUserMapWindowPoints( 0, info.hwndCapture, &pt, 1, 0 );
+    if (NtUserGetClientRect( info.hwndCapture, &rect, 0 ) && PtInRect( &rect, pt )) return;
+    TRACE( "click outside the capture window %p at %s\n", info.hwndCapture, wine_dbgstr_point( &pt ) );
+    NtUserPostMessage( info.hwndCapture, WM_LBUTTONDOWN, MK_LBUTTON, MAKELPARAM( pt.x, pt.y ) );
+    NtUserPostMessage( info.hwndCapture, WM_LBUTTONUP, 0, MAKELPARAM( pt.x, pt.y ) );
+}
+
 /**********************************************************************
  *              focus_out
  */
@@ -880,6 +903,7 @@ static void focus_out( Display *display , HWND hwnd )
 
     if (is_virtual_desktop()) return;
     if (hwnd != NtUserGetForegroundWindow()) return;
+    click_outside_capture();
     if (!(NtUserGetWindowLongW( hwnd, GWL_STYLE ) & WS_MINIMIZE))
         send_message( hwnd, WM_CANCELMODE, 0, 0 );
 
